    },
    "On your %@ only. MUSQ has no account and doesn't upload your workouts. Deleting the app deletes them, so keep it installed (or back up your %@) to keep your history." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "vi" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Chỉ trên %@ của bạn. MUSQ không có tài khoản và không tải các buổi tập của bạn lên mạng. Xoá ứng dụng sẽ xoá luôn dữ liệu này, vì vậy hãy giữ ứng dụng (hoặc sao lưu %@) để giữ lại lịch sử tập."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "On your %@. MUSQ doesn't upload your workouts or keep them on a server. The optional Premium AI features are the exception: when you use one, what it needs goes to MUSQ's server and OpenAI, and you're asked first. Signing in with Apple is needed only for them. Deleting the app deletes your workouts, so keep it installed (or back up your %@) to keep your history." : {
      "comment" : "The text for the data section of the FAQ.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "On your %1$@. MUSQ doesn't upload your workouts or keep them on a server. The optional Premium AI features are the exception: when you use one, what it needs goes to MUSQ's server and OpenAI, and you're asked first. Signing in with Apple is needed only for them. Deleting the app deletes your workouts, so keep it installed (or back up your %2$@) to keep your history."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "once" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "vi" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "một lần"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Once 8 finished weeks have a Balance and weigh-ins, MUSQ sets your better-balanced weeks against the rest, so you can see what moves your weight." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the comparison of the user's weeks.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Once every group in your split has been trained, a new round starts and each turns green again as it recovers." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "vi" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Khi mọi nhóm trong lịch tập của bạn đã được tập, một vòng mới bắt đầu và mỗi nhóm lại chuyển sang xanh lá khi đã phục hồi."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Once you connect it in Profile › Settings › Apple Health, MUSQ reads your steps, walking distance, active energy, sleep and workouts, and never writes to Health. Steps and last night's sleep show on Today, with their trends in Progress. Your average steps over the last %@ full days (at least %@ needed) set how active your days are in the calorie plan, in place of your answer to the daily-activity question; steps during your logged MUSQ workouts don't count, since your training days already do. You can stop steps setting the plan on the same screen. Active energy is shown beside your calorie target but never added to it. What MUSQ reads stays on your %@: the readings are never saved, and never sent to MUSQ or advertisers. Only your step and sleep goals and the calorie-plan switch are kept with your settings, plus, while your steps set the plan, the activity level they last set. To stop MUSQ reading Apple Health, go to Settings › Privacy & Security › Health › MUSQ (or in the Health app, tap your picture › Apps › MUSQ)." : {
      "comment" : "The text is the same, but with",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Once you connect it in Profile › Settings › Apple Health, MUSQ reads your steps, walking distance, active energy, sleep and workouts, and never writes to Health. Steps and last night's sleep show on Today, with their trends in Progress. Your average steps over the last %1$@ full days (at least %2$@ needed) set how active your days are in the calorie plan, in place of your answer to the daily-activity question; steps during your logged MUSQ workouts don't count, since your training days already do. You can stop steps setting the plan on the same screen. Active energy is shown beside your calorie target but never added to it. What MUSQ reads stays on your %3$@: the readings are never saved, and never sent to MUSQ or advertisers. Only your step and sleep goals and the calorie-plan switch are kept with your settings, plus, while your steps set the plan, the activity level they last set. To stop MUSQ reading Apple Health, go to Settings › Privacy & Security › Health › MUSQ (or in the Health app, tap your picture › Apps › MUSQ)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Once you connect it in Profile › Settings › Apple Health, MUSQ reads your steps, walking distance, active energy, sleep and workouts, and never writes to Health. Steps and last night's sleep show on Today, with their trends in Progress. Your average steps over the last %@ full days (at least %@ needed) set how active your days are in the calorie plan, in place of your answer to the daily-activity question; steps during your logged MUSQ workouts don't count, since your training days already do. You can stop steps setting the plan on the same screen. Active energy is shown beside your calorie target but never added to it. What MUSQ reads stays on your %@: the readings are never saved, and never sent to MUSQ or advertisers. The one exception is yours to make: sleep is never sent to the AI coach unless you choose to include it in a question about your Balance; it then goes, through MUSQ's server and OpenAI, with that question and the next ones in the chat, and stays in the chat on your %@, never in backups, until you clear it. Only your step and sleep goals and the calorie-plan switch are kept with your settings, plus, while your steps set the plan, the activity level they last set. To stop MUSQ reading Apple Health, go to Settings › Privacy & Security › Health › MUSQ (or in the Health app, tap your picture › Apps › MUSQ)." : {
      "comment" : "Text for the Apple Health section of the FAQ.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Once you connect it in Profile › Settings › Apple Health, MUSQ reads your steps, walking distance, active energy, sleep and workouts, and never writes to Health. Steps and last night's sleep show on Today, with their trends in Progress. Your average steps over the last %1$@ full days (at least %2$@ needed) set how active your days are in the calorie plan, in place of your answer to the daily-activity question; steps during your logged MUSQ workouts don't count, since your training days already do. You can stop steps setting the plan on the same screen. Active energy is shown beside your calorie target but never added to it. What MUSQ reads stays on your %3$@: the readings are never saved, and never sent to MUSQ or advertisers. The one exception is yours to make: sleep is never sent to the AI coach unless you choose to include it in a question about your Balance; it then goes, through MUSQ's server and OpenAI, with that question and the next ones in the chat, and stays in the chat on your %4$@, never in backups, until you clear it. Only your step and sleep goals and the calorie-plan switch are kept with your settings, plus, while your steps set the plan, the activity level they last set. To stop MUSQ reading Apple Health, go to Settings › Privacy & Security › Health › MUSQ (or in the Health app, tap your picture › Apps › MUSQ)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One corner per pillar: a weak one pulls its corner in." : {
      "comment" : "Text describing the triangle-style Balance card.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "One dial counts the day's goals and says what to do next." : {
      "comment" : "Description of the Today layout option that shows a dial with the day's goals and a message for the next step.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "One payment, Premium for good" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "vi" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Thanh toán một lần, Premium mãi mãi"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One payment. No subscription." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "vi" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Thanh toán một lần. Không đăng ký định kỳ."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One picture of your last 7 days in three parts. Train: showing up on your training days, and enough weekly sets for each muscle in your split. Eat: protein, eating against your plan and water, from your meal log or a two-tap evening check-in. Sleep: time asleep against your goal and how regular it is, from Apple Health or your own “Slept about…”. Balance is half the average of the parts it can score plus half the weakest, so lifting the weakest moves it most. It shows once two parts are scored, and a part with no data shows as not tracked, never as zero. The weakest part is your lever, with one thing to do today. It rates what you do, not your results: your weight or key lifts sit beside it. In Profile › Settings › Balance you can pick its look, stop scoring eating or sleep, hide calorie numbers, turn on its reminders, and pause a week of illness, travel or a deload. The score is worked out on your %@ and never saved." : {
      "comment" : "Text for the Balance section of the FAQ.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "One ring in three parts, your Balance in the middle." : {
      "comment" : "Text describing the balance card style that looks like a ring.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "One set at a time." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "vi" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Từng hiệp một."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One workout at a time." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "vi" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Từng buổi tập một."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Only an anonymous ID goes with it, so OpenAI can spot abuse: not your name, workouts, body measurements or health answers." : {
      "comment" : "Text in the consent sheet for the meal feature.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Only sets marked Done count toward your muscle history." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "vi" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Chỉ những hiệp đã đánh dấu Đã xong mới được tính vào lịch sử tập của nhóm cơ."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Only sets you mark done. Planned but unfinished sets never count toward recovery, records or history." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "vi" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Chỉ những hiệp bạn đánh dấu đã xong. Các hiệp đã lên kế hoạch nhưng chưa hoàn thành sẽ không bao giờ được tính vào phục hồi, kỷ lục hay lịch sử."
          }
        }
      }
    },
